  "title": "Erdős Problem #1005",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\frac{a_1}{b_1},\\frac{a_2}{b_2},\\ldots$ be the Farey fractions of order $n\\geq 4$. Let $f(n)$ be the largest integer such that if $1\\leq k<l\\leq k+f(n)$ then $\\frac{a_k}{b_k}$ and $\\frac{a_l}{b_l}$ are similarly ordered - in other words, $ (a_k-a_l)(b_k-b_l)\\geq 0. $ Estimate $f(n)$ - in particular, is there a constant $c>0$ such that $f(n)=(c+o(1))n$ for all large $n$?",
    "sha256": "78421f319c8e764ec861d2e6a8241636a85614ec9d436c43cab7d7a6a46d8d58",
